THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

geky/gf256 - https://github.com/geky/gf256
Copyright C. Haster and contributors. BSD-3-Clause.

The GF(2^8) arithmetic in api/rust/custody-core/src/gf256.rs, which underpins
Shamir secret sharing for custody, takes its design and algorithms from
geky/gf256. Horizon's implementation was independently rewritten and adapted
for constant-time operation: no branches on field elements, no secret-indexed
memory access, and no early return on a field-element value. It is validated
against reference arithmetic by exhaustive testing of all 65 536 operand
pairs, property tests, fuzzing, and inspection of the compiled output.

Re-implementing a published algorithm does not necessarily make the result a
derivative work in the copyright sense, and no code was copied. The credit is
recorded anyway because it states where the technical choice came from: an
auditor who notices the conceptual resemblance should find the provenance
declared rather than have to wonder about it. BSD-3-Clause is compatible with
AGPL-3.0-or-later, and geky/gf256 has carried that license throughout.

